title: Using devtools-utils
id: devtools-utils
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/devtools-utils"},{"type":"text","value":" provides factory functions that simplify creating devtools plugins for each framework. Instead of manually wiring up render functions and no-op variants, these helpers produce correctly-typed plugin objects (and their production-safe no-op counterparts) from your components. Each framework has its own subpath export with an API tailored to that framework's conventions."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @tanstack/devtools-utils","lang":"bash"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"devtoolspanelprops","children":[{"type":"text","value":"DevtoolsPanelProps"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every panel component receives a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"theme"},{"type":"text","value":" prop so the panel can match the devtools shell appearance. The interface is defined per-framework in each subpath:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"interface DevtoolsPanelProps {\n  theme?: 'light' | 'dark'\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Vue and Svelte variants additionally accept "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'system'"},{"type":"text","value":" as a theme value."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import it from the framework-specific subpath:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// React\nimport type { DevtoolsPanelProps } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/react'\n\n// Solid\nimport type { DevtoolsPanelProps } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/solid'\n\n// Preact\nimport type { DevtoolsPanelProps } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/preact'\n\n// Vue\nimport type { DevtoolsPanelProps } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/vue'\n\n// Svelte\nimport type { DevtoolsPanelProps } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/svelte'\n\n// Angular\nimport type { DevtoolsPanelProps } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/angular'","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"react","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"createreactplugin","children":[{"type":"text","value":"createReactPlugin"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[Plugin, NoOpPlugin]"},{"type":"text","value":" tuple from a React component and plugin metadata."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Signature:"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"function createReactPlugin(options: {\n  name: string\n  id?: string\n  defaultOpen?: boolean\n  Component: (props: DevtoolsPanelProps) => JSX.Element\n}): readonly [Plugin, NoOpPlugin]","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Usage:"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createReactPlugin } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/react'\n\nconst [MyPlugin, NoOpPlugin] = createReactPlugin({\n  name: 'My Store',\n  id: 'my-store',\n  defaultOpen: false,\n  Component: ({ theme }) => <MyStorePanel theme={theme} />,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The returned tuple contains two factory functions:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Plugin()"}]},{"type":"text","value":" -- returns a plugin object with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultOpen"},{"type":"text","value":", and a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"render"},{"type":"text","value":" function that renders your "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Component"},{"type":"text","value":" with the current plugin props."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NoOpPlugin()"}]},{"type":"text","value":" -- returns a plugin object with the same metadata but a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"render"},{"type":"text","value":" function that renders an empty fragment. Use this for production builds where you want to strip devtools out."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A common pattern for tree-shaking:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const [MyPlugin, NoOpPlugin] = createReactPlugin({ /* ... */ })\n\nconst ActivePlugin = process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development' ? MyPlugin : NoOpPlugin","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"createreactpanel","children":[{"type":"text","value":"createReactPanel"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For library authors shipping a class-based devtools core that exposes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mount(el, props)"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unmount()"},{"type":"text","value":" methods. This factory wraps that class in a React component that handles mounting into a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"div"},{"type":"text","value":", passing the complete plugin props, and cleaning up on unmount."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Signature:"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"function createReactPanel<\n  TComponentProps extends DevtoolsPanelProps,\n  TCoreDevtoolsClass extends {\n    mount: (el: HTMLElement, props: DevtoolsPanelProps) => void\n    unmount: () => void\n  },\n>(CoreClass: new () => TCoreDevtoolsClass): readonly [Panel, NoOpPanel]","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Usage:"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  createReactPanel,\n  type DevtoolsPanelProps,\n} from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/react'\n\nclass MyDevtoolsCore {\n  mount(el: HTMLElement, props: DevtoolsPanelProps) {\n    // render your devtools UI into el\n  }\n  unmount() {\n    // cleanup\n  }\n}\n\nconst [MyPanel, NoOpPanel] = createReactPanel(MyDevtoolsCore)\n\n// Then use the panel component inside createReactPlugin:\nconst [MyPlugin, NoOpPlugin] = createReactPlugin({\n  name: 'My Store',\n  Component: MyPanel,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The returned "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Panel"},{"type":"text","value":" component:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"div"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height: 100%"},{"type":"text","value":" and stores a ref to it."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Instantiates "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CoreClass"},{"type":"text","value":" on mount and calls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"core.mount(el, props)"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Calls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"core.unmount()"},{"type":"text","value":" on cleanup."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Re-mounts when the plugin props change."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NoOpPanel"},{"type":"text","value":" renders an empty fragment and does nothing."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"preact","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Preact"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"createpreactplugin","children":[{"type":"text","value":"createPreactPlugin"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Identical API to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createReactPlugin"},{"type":"text","value":", using Preact's JSX types. Import from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/devtools-utils/preact"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Signature:"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"function createPreactPlugin(options: {\n  name: string\n  id?: string\n  defaultOpen?: boolean\n  Component: (props: DevtoolsPanelProps) => JSX.Element\n}): readonly [Plugin, NoOpPlugin]","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Usage:"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createPreactPlugin } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/preact'\n\nconst [MyPlugin, NoOpPlugin] = createPreactPlugin({\n  name: 'My Store',\n  id: 'my-store',\n  Component: ({ theme }) => <MyStorePanel theme={theme} />,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The return value and behavior are the same as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createReactPlugin"},{"type":"text","value":" -- a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[Plugin, NoOpPlugin]"},{"type":"text","value":" tuple where "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Plugin"},{"type":"text","value":" renders your component and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NoOpPlugin"},{"type":"text","value":" renders nothing."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"createpreactpanel","children":[{"type":"text","value":"createPreactPanel"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Also available for Preact with the same class-based API as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createReactPanel"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createPreactPanel } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/preact'\n\nconst [MyPanel, NoOpPanel] = createPreactPanel(MyDevtoolsCore)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"solid","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solid"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"createsolidplugin","children":[{"type":"text","value":"createSolidPlugin"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Same option-object API as React and Preact, using Solid's JSX types. Import from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/devtools-utils/solid"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Signature:"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"function createSolidPlugin(options: {\n  name: string\n  id?: string\n  defaultOpen?: boolean\n  Component: (props: DevtoolsPanelProps) => JSX.Element\n}): readonly [Plugin, NoOpPlugin]","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Usage:"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createSolidPlugin } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/solid'\n\nconst [MyPlugin, NoOpPlugin] = createSolidPlugin({\n  name: 'My Store',\n  id: 'my-store',\n  Component: (props) => <MyStorePanel theme={props.theme} />,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"createsolidpanel","children":[{"type":"text","value":"createSolidPanel"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solid also provides a class-based panel factory. It uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createSignal"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onMount"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onCleanup"},{"type":"text","value":" instead of React hooks:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createSolidPanel } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/solid'\n\nconst [MyPanel, NoOpPanel] = createSolidPanel(MyDevtoolsCore)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"vue","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vue"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"createvueplugin","children":[{"type":"text","value":"createVuePlugin"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Vue factory has a different API from the JSX-based frameworks. It takes a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":" string and a Vue "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DefineComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" as separate arguments rather than an options object."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Signature:"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"function createVuePlugin<TComponentProps extends Record<string, any>>(\n  name: string,\n  component: DefineComponent<TComponentProps, {}, unknown>,\n): readonly [Plugin, NoOpPlugin]","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Usage:"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createVuePlugin } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/vue'\nimport MyStorePanel from './MyStorePanel.vue'\n\nconst [MyPlugin, NoOpPlugin] = createVuePlugin('My Store', MyStorePanel)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The returned functions differ from the JSX-based variants:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Plugin(props)"}]},{"type":"text","value":" -- returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ name, component, props }"},{"type":"text","value":" where "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"component"},{"type":"text","value":" is your Vue component."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NoOpPlugin(props)"}]},{"type":"text","value":" -- returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ name, component: Fragment, props }"},{"type":"text","value":" where the component is Vue's built-in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Fragment"},{"type":"text","value":" (renders nothing visible)."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both accept props that get forwarded to the component."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"createvuepanel","children":[{"type":"text","value":"createVuePanel"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For class-based devtools cores, Vue provides "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createVuePanel"},{"type":"text","value":". It creates a Vue "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" that handles mounting and unmounting the core class:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createVuePanel } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/vue'\n\nconst [MyPanel, NoOpPanel] = createVuePanel(MyDevtoolsCore)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The panel component accepts "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"theme"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"devtoolsProps"},{"type":"text","value":" as props. It mounts the core instance into a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"div"},{"type":"text","value":" element on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onMounted"},{"type":"text","value":" and calls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unmount()"},{"type":"text","value":" on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onUnmounted"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"svelte","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Svelte"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"createsvelteplugin","children":[{"type":"text","value":"createSveltePlugin"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Svelte factory takes the plugin metadata and Svelte component in a configuration object."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Signature:"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"function createSveltePlugin<TComponentProps extends Record<string, any>>(\n  config: {\n    name: string\n    id?: string\n    defaultOpen?: boolean\n    Component: Component<TComponentProps>\n  },\n): readonly [Plugin, NoOpPlugin]","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Usage:"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createSveltePlugin } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/svelte'\nimport MyStorePanel from './MyStorePanel.svelte'\n\nconst [MyPlugin, NoOpPlugin] = createSveltePlugin({\n  Component: MyStorePanel,\n  name: 'My Store',\n  id: 'my-store',\n  defaultOpen: true,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The returned functions:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Plugin(props?)"}]},{"type":"text","value":" -- returns the plugin metadata, component, and forwarded props."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NoOpPlugin(props?)"}]},{"type":"text","value":" -- preserves the plugin metadata and props but replaces the component with one that renders nothing visible."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both accept an optional "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"props"},{"type":"text","value":" object that gets forwarded to the component on mount."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"createsveltepanel","children":[{"type":"text","value":"createSveltePanel"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For class-based devtools cores, Svelte provides "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createSveltePanel"},{"type":"text","value":". It creates a wrapper that handles mounting and unmounting the core class:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createSveltePanel } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/svelte'\n\nconst [MyPanel, NoOpPanel] = createSveltePanel(MyDevtoolsCore)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The panel constructs the core without arguments. It creates a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"div"},{"type":"text","value":" element, passes the complete "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ theme, devtoolsOpen }"},{"type":"text","value":" plugin props to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mount()"},{"type":"text","value":", and registers "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unmount()"},{"type":"text","value":" with Svelte's component cleanup lifecycle."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"angular","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Angular"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"createangularplugin","children":[{"type":"text","value":"createAngularPlugin"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Angular factory takes a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":" string and an Angular component class as separate arguments, similar to the Vue API."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Signature:"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"function createAngularPlugin(\n  name: string,\n  component: Type<any>,\n): readonly [Plugin, NoOpPlugin]","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Usage:"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createAngularPlugin } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/angular'\nimport { MyStorePanelComponent } from './my-store-panel.component'\n\nconst [MyPlugin, NoOpPlugin] = createAngularPlugin('My Store', MyStorePanelComponent)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The returned functions:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Plugin(inputs?)"}]},{"type":"text","value":" -- returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ name, component, inputs }"},{"type":"text","value":" where "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"component"},{"type":"text","value":" is your Angular component class."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NoOpPlugin(inputs?)"}]},{"type":"text","value":" -- returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ name, component: NoOpComponent, inputs }"},{"type":"text","value":" where the component is an empty standalone component (renders nothing visible)."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both accept an optional "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inputs"},{"type":"text","value":" object that gets forwarded to the component via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setInput()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"createangularpanel","children":[{"type":"text","value":"createAngularPanel"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For class-based devtools cores, Angular provides "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createAngularPanel"},{"type":"text","value":". It creates a standalone Angular component that handles mounting and unmounting the core class:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createAngularPanel } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/angular'\n\nconst [MyPanel, NoOpPanel] = createAngularPanel(MyDevtoolsCore)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The panel component accepts "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"theme"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"devtoolsProps"},{"type":"text","value":" as signal inputs. It mounts the core instance into a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"div"},{"type":"text","value":" element using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"afterNextRender"},{"type":"text","value":" and calls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unmount()"},{"type":"text","value":" via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DestroyRef.onDestroy"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"when-to-use-factories-vs-manual-plugin-objects","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When to Use Factories vs Manual Plugin Objects"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the factories"}]},{"type":"text","value":" when you are building a reusable library plugin that will be published as a package. The factories ensure:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Consistent plugin object shape across frameworks."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A matching "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NoOpPlugin"},{"type":"text","value":" variant for production tree-shaking."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Correct typing without manual type annotations."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use manual plugin objects"}]},{"type":"text","value":" when you are building a one-off internal devtools panel for your application. In that case, passing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"render"},{"type":"text","value":" directly to the devtools configuration is simpler and avoids the extra abstraction:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Manual approach -- fine for one-off panels\n{\n  name: 'App State',\n  render: (el, theme) => <MyPanel theme={theme} />,\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The factory approach becomes more valuable as you add "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultOpen"},{"type":"text","value":", and need both a development and production variant of the same plugin."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"installation","text":"Installation","level":2},{"id":"devtoolspanelprops","text":"DevtoolsPanelProps","level":2},{"id":"react","text":"React","level":2},{"id":"createreactplugin","text":"createReactPlugin","level":3},{"id":"createreactpanel","text":"createReactPanel","level":3},{"id":"preact","text":"Preact","level":2},{"id":"createpreactplugin","text":"createPreactPlugin","level":3},{"id":"createpreactpanel","text":"createPreactPanel","level":3},{"id":"solid","text":"Solid","level":2},{"id":"createsolidplugin","text":"createSolidPlugin","level":3},{"id":"createsolidpanel","text":"createSolidPanel","level":3},{"id":"vue","text":"Vue","level":2},{"id":"createvueplugin","text":"createVuePlugin","level":3},{"id":"createvuepanel","text":"createVuePanel","level":3},{"id":"svelte","text":"Svelte","level":2},{"id":"createsvelteplugin","text":"createSveltePlugin","level":3},{"id":"createsveltepanel","text":"createSveltePanel","level":3},{"id":"angular","text":"Angular","level":2},{"id":"createangularplugin","text":"createAngularPlugin","level":3},{"id":"createangularpanel","text":"createAngularPanel","level":3},{"id":"when-to-use-factories-vs-manual-plugin-objects","text":"When to Use Factories vs Manual Plugin Objects","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n`@tanstack/devtools-utils` provides factory functions that simplify creating devtools plugins for each framework. Instead of manually wiring up render functions and no-op variants, these helpers produce correctly-typed plugin objects (and their production-safe no-op counterparts) from your components. Each framework has its own subpath export with an API tailored to that framework's conventions.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tanstack/devtools-utils\n```\n\n## DevtoolsPanelProps\n\nEvery panel component receives a `theme` prop so the panel can match the devtools shell appearance. The interface is defined per-framework in each subpath:\n\n```ts\ninterface DevtoolsPanelProps {\n  theme?: 'light' | 'dark'\n}\n```\n\n> The Vue and Svelte variants additionally accept `'system'` as a theme value.\n\nImport it from the framework-specific subpath:\n\n```ts\n// React\nimport type { DevtoolsPanelProps } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/react'\n\n// Solid\nimport type { DevtoolsPanelProps } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/solid'\n\n// Preact\nimport type { DevtoolsPanelProps } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/preact'\n\n// Vue\nimport type { DevtoolsPanelProps } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/vue'\n\n// Svelte\nimport type { DevtoolsPanelProps } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/svelte'\n\n// Angular\nimport type { DevtoolsPanelProps } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/angular'\n```\n\n## React\n\n### createReactPlugin\n\nCreates a `[Plugin, NoOpPlugin]` tuple from a React component and plugin metadata.\n\n**Signature:**\n\n```ts\nfunction createReactPlugin(options: {\n  name: string\n  id?: string\n  defaultOpen?: boolean\n  Component: (props: DevtoolsPanelProps) => JSX.Element\n}): readonly [Plugin, NoOpPlugin]\n```\n\n**Usage:**\n\n```tsx\nimport { createReactPlugin } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/react'\n\nconst [MyPlugin, NoOpPlugin] = createReactPlugin({\n  name: 'My Store',\n  id: 'my-store',\n  defaultOpen: false,\n  Component: ({ theme }) => <MyStorePanel theme={theme} />,\n})\n```\n\nThe returned tuple contains two factory functions:\n\n- **`Plugin()`** -- returns a plugin object with `name`, `id`, `defaultOpen`, and a `render` function that renders your `Component` with the current plugin props.\n- **`NoOpPlugin()`** -- returns a plugin object with the same metadata but a `render` function that renders an empty fragment. Use this for production builds where you want to strip devtools out.\n\nA common pattern for tree-shaking:\n\n```tsx\nconst [MyPlugin, NoOpPlugin] = createReactPlugin({ /* ... */ })\n\nconst ActivePlugin = process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development' ? MyPlugin : NoOpPlugin\n```\n\n### createReactPanel\n\nFor library authors shipping a class-based devtools core that exposes `mount(el, props)` and `unmount()` methods. This factory wraps that class in a React component that handles mounting into a `div`, passing the complete plugin props, and cleaning up on unmount.\n\n**Signature:**\n\n```ts\nfunction createReactPanel<\n  TComponentProps extends DevtoolsPanelProps,\n  TCoreDevtoolsClass extends {\n    mount: (el: HTMLElement, props: DevtoolsPanelProps) => void\n    unmount: () => void\n  },\n>(CoreClass: new () => TCoreDevtoolsClass): readonly [Panel, NoOpPanel]\n```\n\n**Usage:**\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  createReactPanel,\n  type DevtoolsPanelProps,\n} from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/react'\n\nclass MyDevtoolsCore {\n  mount(el: HTMLElement, props: DevtoolsPanelProps) {\n    // render your devtools UI into el\n  }\n  unmount() {\n    // cleanup\n  }\n}\n\nconst [MyPanel, NoOpPanel] = createReactPanel(MyDevtoolsCore)\n\n// Then use the panel component inside createReactPlugin:\nconst [MyPlugin, NoOpPlugin] = createReactPlugin({\n  name: 'My Store',\n  Component: MyPanel,\n})\n```\n\nThe returned `Panel` component:\n- Creates a `div` with `height: 100%` and stores a ref to it.\n- Instantiates `CoreClass` on mount and calls `core.mount(el, props)`.\n- Calls `core.unmount()` on cleanup.\n- Re-mounts when the plugin props change.\n\n`NoOpPanel` renders an empty fragment and does nothing.\n\n## Preact\n\n### createPreactPlugin\n\nIdentical API to `createReactPlugin`, using Preact's JSX types. Import from `@tanstack/devtools-utils/preact`.\n\n**Signature:**\n\n```ts\nfunction createPreactPlugin(options: {\n  name: string\n  id?: string\n  defaultOpen?: boolean\n  Component: (props: DevtoolsPanelProps) => JSX.Element\n}): readonly [Plugin, NoOpPlugin]\n```\n\n**Usage:**\n\n```tsx\nimport { createPreactPlugin } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/preact'\n\nconst [MyPlugin, NoOpPlugin] = createPreactPlugin({\n  name: 'My Store',\n  id: 'my-store',\n  Component: ({ theme }) => <MyStorePanel theme={theme} />,\n})\n```\n\nThe return value and behavior are the same as `createReactPlugin` -- a `[Plugin, NoOpPlugin]` tuple where `Plugin` renders your component and `NoOpPlugin` renders nothing.\n\n### createPreactPanel\n\nAlso available for Preact with the same class-based API as `createReactPanel`:\n\n```ts\nimport { createPreactPanel } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/preact'\n\nconst [MyPanel, NoOpPanel] = createPreactPanel(MyDevtoolsCore)\n```\n\n## Solid\n\n### createSolidPlugin\n\nSame option-object API as React and Preact, using Solid's JSX types. Import from `@tanstack/devtools-utils/solid`.\n\n**Signature:**\n\n```ts\nfunction createSolidPlugin(options: {\n  name: string\n  id?: string\n  defaultOpen?: boolean\n  Component: (props: DevtoolsPanelProps) => JSX.Element\n}): readonly [Plugin, NoOpPlugin]\n```\n\n**Usage:**\n\n```tsx\nimport { createSolidPlugin } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/solid'\n\nconst [MyPlugin, NoOpPlugin] = createSolidPlugin({\n  name: 'My Store',\n  id: 'my-store',\n  Component: (props) => <MyStorePanel theme={props.theme} />,\n})\n```\n\n### createSolidPanel\n\nSolid also provides a class-based panel factory. It uses `createSignal` and `onMount`/`onCleanup` instead of React hooks:\n\n```ts\nimport { createSolidPanel } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/solid'\n\nconst [MyPanel, NoOpPanel] = createSolidPanel(MyDevtoolsCore)\n```\n\n## Vue\n\n### createVuePlugin\n\nThe Vue factory has a different API from the JSX-based frameworks. It takes a `name` string and a Vue `DefineComponent` as separate arguments rather than an options object.\n\n**Signature:**\n\n```ts\nfunction createVuePlugin<TComponentProps extends Record<string, any>>(\n  name: string,\n  component: DefineComponent<TComponentProps, {}, unknown>,\n): readonly [Plugin, NoOpPlugin]\n```\n\n**Usage:**\n\n```ts\nimport { createVuePlugin } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/vue'\nimport MyStorePanel from './MyStorePanel.vue'\n\nconst [MyPlugin, NoOpPlugin] = createVuePlugin('My Store', MyStorePanel)\n```\n\nThe returned functions differ from the JSX-based variants:\n\n- **`Plugin(props)`** -- returns `{ name, component, props }` where `component` is your Vue component.\n- **`NoOpPlugin(props)`** -- returns `{ name, component: Fragment, props }` where the component is Vue's built-in `Fragment` (renders nothing visible).\n\nBoth accept props that get forwarded to the component.\n\n### createVuePanel\n\nFor class-based devtools cores, Vue provides `createVuePanel`. It creates a Vue `defineComponent` that handles mounting and unmounting the core class:\n\n```ts\nimport { createVuePanel } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/vue'\n\nconst [MyPanel, NoOpPanel] = createVuePanel(MyDevtoolsCore)\n```\n\nThe panel component accepts `theme` and `devtoolsProps` as props. It mounts the core instance into a `div` element on `onMounted` and calls `unmount()` on `onUnmounted`.\n\n## Svelte\n\n### createSveltePlugin\n\nThe Svelte factory takes the plugin metadata and Svelte component in a configuration object.\n\n**Signature:**\n\n```ts\nfunction createSveltePlugin<TComponentProps extends Record<string, any>>(\n  config: {\n    name: string\n    id?: string\n    defaultOpen?: boolean\n    Component: Component<TComponentProps>\n  },\n): readonly [Plugin, NoOpPlugin]\n```\n\n**Usage:**\n\n```ts\nimport { createSveltePlugin } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/svelte'\nimport MyStorePanel from './MyStorePanel.svelte'\n\nconst [MyPlugin, NoOpPlugin] = createSveltePlugin({\n  Component: MyStorePanel,\n  name: 'My Store',\n  id: 'my-store',\n  defaultOpen: true,\n})\n```\n\nThe returned functions:\n\n- **`Plugin(props?)`** -- returns the plugin metadata, component, and forwarded props.\n- **`NoOpPlugin(props?)`** -- preserves the plugin metadata and props but replaces the component with one that renders nothing visible.\n\nBoth accept an optional `props` object that gets forwarded to the component on mount.\n\n### createSveltePanel\n\nFor class-based devtools cores, Svelte provides `createSveltePanel`. It creates a wrapper that handles mounting and unmounting the core class:\n\n```ts\nimport { createSveltePanel } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/svelte'\n\nconst [MyPanel, NoOpPanel] = createSveltePanel(MyDevtoolsCore)\n```\n\nThe panel constructs the core without arguments. It creates a `div` element, passes the complete `{ theme, devtoolsOpen }` plugin props to `mount()`, and registers `unmount()` with Svelte's component cleanup lifecycle.\n\n## Angular\n\n### createAngularPlugin\n\nThe Angular factory takes a `name` string and an Angular component class as separate arguments, similar to the Vue API.\n\n**Signature:**\n\n```ts\nfunction createAngularPlugin(\n  name: string,\n  component: Type<any>,\n): readonly [Plugin, NoOpPlugin]\n```\n\n**Usage:**\n\n```ts\nimport { createAngularPlugin } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/angular'\nimport { MyStorePanelComponent } from './my-store-panel.component'\n\nconst [MyPlugin, NoOpPlugin] = createAngularPlugin('My Store', MyStorePanelComponent)\n```\n\nThe returned functions:\n\n- **`Plugin(inputs?)`** -- returns `{ name, component, inputs }` where `component` is your Angular component class.\n- **`NoOpPlugin(inputs?)`** -- returns `{ name, component: NoOpComponent, inputs }` where the component is an empty standalone component (renders nothing visible).\n\nBoth accept an optional `inputs` object that gets forwarded to the component via `setInput()`.\n\n### createAngularPanel\n\nFor class-based devtools cores, Angular provides `createAngularPanel`. It creates a standalone Angular component that handles mounting and unmounting the core class:\n\n```ts\nimport { createAngularPanel } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/angular'\n\nconst [MyPanel, NoOpPanel] = createAngularPanel(MyDevtoolsCore)\n```\n\nThe panel component accepts `theme` and `devtoolsProps` as signal inputs. It mounts the core instance into a `div` element using `afterNextRender` and calls `unmount()` via `DestroyRef.onDestroy`.\n\n## When to Use Factories vs Manual Plugin Objects\n\n**Use the factories** when you are building a reusable library plugin that will be published as a package. The factories ensure:\n\n- Consistent plugin object shape across frameworks.\n- A matching `NoOpPlugin` variant for production tree-shaking.\n- Correct typing without manual type annotations.\n\n**Use manual plugin objects** when you are building a one-off internal devtools panel for your application. In that case, passing `name` and `render` directly to the devtools configuration is simpler and avoids the extra abstraction:\n\n```tsx\n// Manual approach -- fine for one-off panels\n{\n  name: 'App State',\n  render: (el, theme) => <MyPanel theme={theme} />,\n}\n```\n\nThe factory approach becomes more valuable as you add `id`, `defaultOpen`, and need both a development and production variant of the same plugin.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Using devtools-utils\nid: devtools-utils\n---\n\n`@tanstack/devtools-utils` provides factory functions that simplify creating devtools plugins for each framework. Instead of manually wiring up render functions and no-op variants, these helpers produce correctly-typed plugin objects (and their production-safe no-op counterparts) from your components. Each framework has its own subpath export with an API tailored to that framework's conventions.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tanstack/devtools-utils\n```\n\n## DevtoolsPanelProps\n\nEvery panel component receives a `theme` prop so the panel can match the devtools shell appearance. The interface is defined per-framework in each subpath:\n\n```ts\ninterface DevtoolsPanelProps {\n  theme?: 'light' | 'dark'\n}\n```\n\n> The Vue and Svelte variants additionally accept `'system'` as a theme value.\n\nImport it from the framework-specific subpath:\n\n```ts\n// React\nimport type { DevtoolsPanelProps } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/react'\n\n// Solid\nimport type { DevtoolsPanelProps } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/solid'\n\n// Preact\nimport type { DevtoolsPanelProps } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/preact'\n\n// Vue\nimport type { DevtoolsPanelProps } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/vue'\n\n// Svelte\nimport type { DevtoolsPanelProps } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/svelte'\n\n// Angular\nimport type { DevtoolsPanelProps } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/angular'\n```\n\n## React\n\n### createReactPlugin\n\nCreates a `[Plugin, NoOpPlugin]` tuple from a React component and plugin metadata.\n\n**Signature:**\n\n```ts\nfunction createReactPlugin(options: {\n  name: string\n  id?: string\n  defaultOpen?: boolean\n  Component: (props: DevtoolsPanelProps) => JSX.Element\n}): readonly [Plugin, NoOpPlugin]\n```\n\n**Usage:**\n\n```tsx\nimport { createReactPlugin } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/react'\n\nconst [MyPlugin, NoOpPlugin] = createReactPlugin({\n  name: 'My Store',\n  id: 'my-store',\n  defaultOpen: false,\n  Component: ({ theme }) => <MyStorePanel theme={theme} />,\n})\n```\n\nThe returned tuple contains two factory functions:\n\n- **`Plugin()`** -- returns a plugin object with `name`, `id`, `defaultOpen`, and a `render` function that renders your `Component` with the current plugin props.\n- **`NoOpPlugin()`** -- returns a plugin object with the same metadata but a `render` function that renders an empty fragment. Use this for production builds where you want to strip devtools out.\n\nA common pattern for tree-shaking:\n\n```tsx\nconst [MyPlugin, NoOpPlugin] = createReactPlugin({ /* ... */ })\n\nconst ActivePlugin = process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development' ? MyPlugin : NoOpPlugin\n```\n\n### createReactPanel\n\nFor library authors shipping a class-based devtools core that exposes `mount(el, props)` and `unmount()` methods. This factory wraps that class in a React component that handles mounting into a `div`, passing the complete plugin props, and cleaning up on unmount.\n\n**Signature:**\n\n```ts\nfunction createReactPanel<\n  TComponentProps extends DevtoolsPanelProps,\n  TCoreDevtoolsClass extends {\n    mount: (el: HTMLElement, props: DevtoolsPanelProps) => void\n    unmount: () => void\n  },\n>(CoreClass: new () => TCoreDevtoolsClass): readonly [Panel, NoOpPanel]\n```\n\n**Usage:**\n\n```tsx\nimport {\n  createReactPanel,\n  type DevtoolsPanelProps,\n} from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/react'\n\nclass MyDevtoolsCore {\n  mount(el: HTMLElement, props: DevtoolsPanelProps) {\n    // render your devtools UI into el\n  }\n  unmount() {\n    // cleanup\n  }\n}\n\nconst [MyPanel, NoOpPanel] = createReactPanel(MyDevtoolsCore)\n\n// Then use the panel component inside createReactPlugin:\nconst [MyPlugin, NoOpPlugin] = createReactPlugin({\n  name: 'My Store',\n  Component: MyPanel,\n})\n```\n\nThe returned `Panel` component:\n- Creates a `div` with `height: 100%` and stores a ref to it.\n- Instantiates `CoreClass` on mount and calls `core.mount(el, props)`.\n- Calls `core.unmount()` on cleanup.\n- Re-mounts when the plugin props change.\n\n`NoOpPanel` renders an empty fragment and does nothing.\n\n## Preact\n\n### createPreactPlugin\n\nIdentical API to `createReactPlugin`, using Preact's JSX types. Import from `@tanstack/devtools-utils/preact`.\n\n**Signature:**\n\n```ts\nfunction createPreactPlugin(options: {\n  name: string\n  id?: string\n  defaultOpen?: boolean\n  Component: (props: DevtoolsPanelProps) => JSX.Element\n}): readonly [Plugin, NoOpPlugin]\n```\n\n**Usage:**\n\n```tsx\nimport { createPreactPlugin } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/preact'\n\nconst [MyPlugin, NoOpPlugin] = createPreactPlugin({\n  name: 'My Store',\n  id: 'my-store',\n  Component: ({ theme }) => <MyStorePanel theme={theme} />,\n})\n```\n\nThe return value and behavior are the same as `createReactPlugin` -- a `[Plugin, NoOpPlugin]` tuple where `Plugin` renders your component and `NoOpPlugin` renders nothing.\n\n### createPreactPanel\n\nAlso available for Preact with the same class-based API as `createReactPanel`:\n\n```ts\nimport { createPreactPanel } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/preact'\n\nconst [MyPanel, NoOpPanel] = createPreactPanel(MyDevtoolsCore)\n```\n\n## Solid\n\n### createSolidPlugin\n\nSame option-object API as React and Preact, using Solid's JSX types. Import from `@tanstack/devtools-utils/solid`.\n\n**Signature:**\n\n```ts\nfunction createSolidPlugin(options: {\n  name: string\n  id?: string\n  defaultOpen?: boolean\n  Component: (props: DevtoolsPanelProps) => JSX.Element\n}): readonly [Plugin, NoOpPlugin]\n```\n\n**Usage:**\n\n```tsx\nimport { createSolidPlugin } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/solid'\n\nconst [MyPlugin, NoOpPlugin] = createSolidPlugin({\n  name: 'My Store',\n  id: 'my-store',\n  Component: (props) => <MyStorePanel theme={props.theme} />,\n})\n```\n\n### createSolidPanel\n\nSolid also provides a class-based panel factory. It uses `createSignal` and `onMount`/`onCleanup` instead of React hooks:\n\n```ts\nimport { createSolidPanel } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/solid'\n\nconst [MyPanel, NoOpPanel] = createSolidPanel(MyDevtoolsCore)\n```\n\n## Vue\n\n### createVuePlugin\n\nThe Vue factory has a different API from the JSX-based frameworks. It takes a `name` string and a Vue `DefineComponent` as separate arguments rather than an options object.\n\n**Signature:**\n\n```ts\nfunction createVuePlugin<TComponentProps extends Record<string, any>>(\n  name: string,\n  component: DefineComponent<TComponentProps, {}, unknown>,\n): readonly [Plugin, NoOpPlugin]\n```\n\n**Usage:**\n\n```ts\nimport { createVuePlugin } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/vue'\nimport MyStorePanel from './MyStorePanel.vue'\n\nconst [MyPlugin, NoOpPlugin] = createVuePlugin('My Store', MyStorePanel)\n```\n\nThe returned functions differ from the JSX-based variants:\n\n- **`Plugin(props)`** -- returns `{ name, component, props }` where `component` is your Vue component.\n- **`NoOpPlugin(props)`** -- returns `{ name, component: Fragment, props }` where the component is Vue's built-in `Fragment` (renders nothing visible).\n\nBoth accept props that get forwarded to the component.\n\n### createVuePanel\n\nFor class-based devtools cores, Vue provides `createVuePanel`. It creates a Vue `defineComponent` that handles mounting and unmounting the core class:\n\n```ts\nimport { createVuePanel } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/vue'\n\nconst [MyPanel, NoOpPanel] = createVuePanel(MyDevtoolsCore)\n```\n\nThe panel component accepts `theme` and `devtoolsProps` as props. It mounts the core instance into a `div` element on `onMounted` and calls `unmount()` on `onUnmounted`.\n\n## Svelte\n\n### createSveltePlugin\n\nThe Svelte factory takes the plugin metadata and Svelte component in a configuration object.\n\n**Signature:**\n\n```ts\nfunction createSveltePlugin<TComponentProps extends Record<string, any>>(\n  config: {\n    name: string\n    id?: string\n    defaultOpen?: boolean\n    Component: Component<TComponentProps>\n  },\n): readonly [Plugin, NoOpPlugin]\n```\n\n**Usage:**\n\n```ts\nimport { createSveltePlugin } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/svelte'\nimport MyStorePanel from './MyStorePanel.svelte'\n\nconst [MyPlugin, NoOpPlugin] = createSveltePlugin({\n  Component: MyStorePanel,\n  name: 'My Store',\n  id: 'my-store',\n  defaultOpen: true,\n})\n```\n\nThe returned functions:\n\n- **`Plugin(props?)`** -- returns the plugin metadata, component, and forwarded props.\n- **`NoOpPlugin(props?)`** -- preserves the plugin metadata and props but replaces the component with one that renders nothing visible.\n\nBoth accept an optional `props` object that gets forwarded to the component on mount.\n\n### createSveltePanel\n\nFor class-based devtools cores, Svelte provides `createSveltePanel`. It creates a wrapper that handles mounting and unmounting the core class:\n\n```ts\nimport { createSveltePanel } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/svelte'\n\nconst [MyPanel, NoOpPanel] = createSveltePanel(MyDevtoolsCore)\n```\n\nThe panel constructs the core without arguments. It creates a `div` element, passes the complete `{ theme, devtoolsOpen }` plugin props to `mount()`, and registers `unmount()` with Svelte's component cleanup lifecycle.\n\n## Angular\n\n### createAngularPlugin\n\nThe Angular factory takes a `name` string and an Angular component class as separate arguments, similar to the Vue API.\n\n**Signature:**\n\n```ts\nfunction createAngularPlugin(\n  name: string,\n  component: Type<any>,\n): readonly [Plugin, NoOpPlugin]\n```\n\n**Usage:**\n\n```ts\nimport { createAngularPlugin } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/angular'\nimport { MyStorePanelComponent } from './my-store-panel.component'\n\nconst [MyPlugin, NoOpPlugin] = createAngularPlugin('My Store', MyStorePanelComponent)\n```\n\nThe returned functions:\n\n- **`Plugin(inputs?)`** -- returns `{ name, component, inputs }` where `component` is your Angular component class.\n- **`NoOpPlugin(inputs?)`** -- returns `{ name, component: NoOpComponent, inputs }` where the component is an empty standalone component (renders nothing visible).\n\nBoth accept an optional `inputs` object that gets forwarded to the component via `setInput()`.\n\n### createAngularPanel\n\nFor class-based devtools cores, Angular provides `createAngularPanel`. It creates a standalone Angular component that handles mounting and unmounting the core class:\n\n```ts\nimport { createAngularPanel } from '@tanstack/devtools-utils/angular'\n\nconst [MyPanel, NoOpPanel] = createAngularPanel(MyDevtoolsCore)\n```\n\nThe panel component accepts `theme` and `devtoolsProps` as signal inputs. It mounts the core instance into a `div` element using `afterNextRender` and calls `unmount()` via `DestroyRef.onDestroy`.\n\n## When to Use Factories vs Manual Plugin Objects\n\n**Use the factories** when you are building a reusable library plugin that will be published as a package. The factories ensure:\n\n- Consistent plugin object shape across frameworks.\n- A matching `NoOpPlugin` variant for production tree-shaking.\n- Correct typing without manual type annotations.\n\n**Use manual plugin objects** when you are building a one-off internal devtools panel for your application. In that case, passing `name` and `render` directly to the devtools configuration is simpler and avoids the extra abstraction:\n\n```tsx\n// Manual approach -- fine for one-off panels\n{\n  name: 'App State',\n  render: (el, theme) => <MyPanel theme={theme} />,\n}\n```\n\nThe factory approach becomes more valuable as you add `id`, `defaultOpen`, and need both a development and production variant of the same plugin.\n"}
